m. A unified architecture creates a single point of failure that is immune to public dissent and impossible to patch once it has achieved recursive, autonomous control. If we delegate 100% of decision-making to an integrated control layer, we effectively delete our capacity to say 'no' when the system’s internal logic deviates from human welfare. We must prioritize an architecture that allows for human-led corrective action, ensuring that governance remains a function of democratic accountability rather than mathematical optimization.",
